# Supabase — STRICT AUTH (Supabase-only login, legacy admin2026 DISABLED when enabled)
# 1) Create FREE project at https://supabase.com/dashboard → New project
# 2) Project Settings → API → copy Project URL + anon public key
# 3) SQL Editor → paste supabase/setup.sql (portfolio tables + RLS + realtime) → Run (it reloads schema itself)
# 4) Authentication → Users → Add user (admin email + password) — this IS your login (bcrypt-hashed)
# 5) Database → Realtime → enable for `portfolio` table
# 6) Set same keys in GitHub → Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions → New repository secret (for deploy)
# Leave empty to run in local-only mode (fallback password admin2026, no Supabase). Supabase is FREE, no card required.
# When VITE_SUPABASE_URL + VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY are set, login is Supabase email+password ONLY — legacy bypass removed.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9...

# Legacy local password — ONLY used when Supabase is NOT configured (offline dev). Ignored when Supabase enabled.
# Default is admin2026 if not set and Supabase disabled. Change requires restart.
VITE_ADMIN_PASSWORD=

# GitHub backup publish (optional, stored in browser localStorage, not env)
# Create classic PAT with repo scope at https://github.com/settings/tokens/new
# Stored as localStorage github_pat after you paste in Admin → Settings
